WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.240
When it comes to popularity versus screen-time,
there may be no bigger winner than Boba Fett.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.070
For decades, fans have been fervently buying
action figures, comics, and novels featuring

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.809
the world's favorite bounty hunter.

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:13.070
Sorry, Dog.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:17.640
People love Fett, even though he has about
four lines of dialogue in the entire Original

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:23.080
Trilogy before being knocked into a giant
pit by a blind guy.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.400
Because of his popularity and his limited
screentime, it would be easy to think that

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.820
Boba Fett doesn't have any hidden secrets.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.329
However, the truth is that there's still plenty
you probably don't know about this mysterious

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:37.040
character from a galaxy far, far away…

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.780
His first real appearance

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.700
Most people know that Boba Fett first appeared
on the big screen in The Empire Strikes Back...

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.850
no matter what George Lucas did to the special
edition of A New Hope later on.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.309
The real savvy fan may even be able to tell
you Fett's first appearance on any screen

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:55.660
was during 1978's Star Wars Holiday Special.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.270
"Maybe I can help you.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.050
I am Boba Fett."

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.379
But neither of those are actually the first
time the public got to see Boba Fett.

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:09.150
His first public appearance was a few weeks
earlier, on September 24, 1978, at the San

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.720
Anselmo County Fair.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.261
San Anselmo was the home of Lucasfilm at the
time and George Lucas thought that taking

00:01:15.261 --> 00:01:17.900
part in the local parade was a great idea.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:23.030
While Fett didn't engage in any pie eating
contests or hog calling, assistant film editor

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:27.920
Duwayne Dunham donned the sweaty costume and
signed autographs — even though no one actually

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.130
knew who Boba Fett was yet.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:31.130
All white

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:36.320
Even before Boba Fett took his unusual place
in a local parade and a terrible holiday special,

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.530
he'd been going through some changes.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:42.750
Concept artist Ralph McQuarrie had a ton of
different designs for Boba that he was testing

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:47.600
out, ultimately settling on the Mandalorian
armor fans know and love today.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:52.170
The original suit was completely fabricated
and screen-tested… except it was completely

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.170
Stormtrooper-white.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:58.040
Sure, he still had a cool jetpack and sinister
visor, but he was basically a bleached-out

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.520
version of the green-and-red guy of today.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.520
Why?

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.270
Those original armor designs were originally
planned to be old Stormtrooper armor from

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:09.399
an old regiment, which would have made him
look like a medieval knight marching into

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:10.720
war with modern soldiers.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.530
But, y'know, in space.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:17.780
As plans for the film shifted and lore began
to grow, the armor became Mandalorian, Fett

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.640
took a smaller role, and he finally got some
much-needed color.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.140
The big bad

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.580
According to an interview with Lucasfilm's
first fan relations officer, Chris Miller,

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:32.030
Fett was originally going to play a much larger
role in the trilogy, which is why he had such

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.360
a prominent role in the Holiday Special.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:41.080
At one point, he was even going to eclipse
Darth Vader as the trilogy's biggest bad guy.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.460
"NOOOOOOOO!"

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:47.990
As George Lucas became increasingly bored
with space, he rewrote Star Wars from a dozen

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:53.370
films down to three, compacted his entire
second trilogy concept into Return of the

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.640
Jedi, and threw Fett into a belching desert
cloaca.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.370
Taking action

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:05.130
When Star Wars has an action figure controversy
— and they happen surprisingly often — it

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:10.040
usually revolves around Leia's gold bikini
or too few Rey figures on the shelves.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:15.070
But the original Star Wars action figure controversy
stemmed from none other than Boba Fett.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.830
"I'm the best bounty hunter in the whole galaxy!"

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.680
"That's why you got the job."

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.930
Let's recap: Fett's first appearance was at
a county fair.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.510
His second appearance was in the Holiday Special.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:30.210
His third appearance, prior to the May 1980
release of Empire Strikes Back, was on the

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:35.790
back of action figure packaging as a mail-away
figure, when he still didn't have a backstory.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:40.390
Just one problem: the Fett figure was portrayed
with a rocket-firing backpack.

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:45.060
Star Wars fans, who were basically the original
turbonerds, were pretty upset at not receiving

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.120
the action-packed Fett they were promised.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.140
Kenner had produced some prototypes of the
full figure, which have since become the Holy

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:55.610
Grail of Star Wars collectibles, but they
were never released to the public due to safety

00:03:55.610 --> 00:04:00.380
concerns after a child choked on a missile
from a Battlestar Galactica toy.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:05.130
Hasbro bought Kenner in 2010, and finally
made things right when they released an actual

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:08.810
rocket-firing Boba Fett as a mail-away in
their Vintage Collection.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:13.750
Finally, adult nerds everywhere got their
fondest wish: death by action figure.

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.579
If they can just figure it out without killing
each other.

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:17.579
"Just push.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.160
Push the button.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:18.660
Push."

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.400
"I'm pushing.

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:21.460
Good God."

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.820
Fett's many origins

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:28.490
Attack of the Clones made it absolutely clear
that Boba Fett is the unaltered clone of legendary

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:33.140
bounty hunter Jango Fett, the prototype for
all of the galaxy's Clone Troopers.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:38.410
Unlike his helmeted clone-bros, Boba is raised
personally by Jango, and eventually takes

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:41.000
his own place in the galaxy as a bounty hunter.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:45.110
But even before Attack of the Clones, the
Star Wars Expanded Universe had developed

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:49.970
a rich backstory for just about every weirdo
in every scene of Star Wars, no matter how

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:50.970
irrelevant.

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.620
Even Ice Cream Maker Guy.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:57.340
Fun fact: his name is Willrow Hood, he's a
Rebel hero, he has his own action figure,

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:02.520
he has a legion of fans, and in terms of screen
time versus fan fervor, he just might beat

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.440
out Boba Fett.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:11.871
Anyway, according to Tales of the Bounty Hunters,
a novel released in 1996, Boba Fett's real

00:05:11.871 --> 00:05:16.620
name was Jaster-Mereel, and he's essentially
an ex-cop from the world known as Concord

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.510
Dawn who's exiled from the planet for killing
his corrupt superior.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:24.660
Eventually, he's taken in by the Mandalorians
and becomes Boba Fett.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:28.550
After Attack of the Clones, however, Jaster
was rewritten to be a completely separate

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.949
character from Fett.

00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:35.130
In the comic series Jango Fett: Open Seasons,
Jaster-Mereel was the leader of Mandalore,

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:39.650
and the guy who took a young Jango Fett under
his wing after Jango's parents were murdered.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:44.330
Occasionally, though, both Boba and Jango
would use Jaster's name as their own, kinda

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:47.220
like an intergalactic Rusty Shackleford.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.470
He's survived a fight with Vader

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:54.550
The Original Trilogy implies that Boba Fett
and Darth Vader have a pretty okay relationship,

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:58.639
but readers of Star Wars comics over the years
have witnessed the rather unforgettable sight

00:05:58.639 --> 00:06:01.930
of Vader and Fett trying to all-out murder
each other.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:05.800
Sure, they're mostly non-canonical now, but
that doesn't mean it's not fun to see.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:11.030
First, there's the fight in Star Wars Tales
#11 where Fett actually holds his own against

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:13.430
Vader in a lightsaber battle in a cantina.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:17.690
Vader and Fett faced off once again in Boba
Fett: Enemy of the Empire #4, where the stakes

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.620
were a bit higher.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:24.100
In truly bizarre comics fashion, the two fight
over the severed-but-still-talkative head

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.229
of a fortune-telling alien queen.

00:06:26.229 --> 00:06:30.370
Boba Fett is hired to retrieve the head in
a box, but Vader wants it as a tool for his

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.060
eventual overthrow of Emperor Palpatine.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:37.770
The two come to blows, with Vader deflecting
blaster bolts and cutting Fett's getaway speeder

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:42.190
in half, until he stops screwing around and
Force chokes Fett... who kicks the head off

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:46.690
a cliff, and jetpacks to safety while Vader
uses the Force to retrieve it.

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:50.940
The two only ended up having a pleasant work
relationship later on because the decapitated

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:56.250
queen-head says they will, and Vader is pretty
superstitious… but they probably also bonded

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:59.990
over how difficult it is to go to the bathroom
while wearing armor.

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:01.500
Eight is enough

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.169
You'd think that Darth Vader would have taken
the record for the most actors portraying

00:07:05.169 --> 00:07:10.540
the same character on the big screen, between
actors, last-second stand-ins, and voice actors,

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:11.890
not to mention stuntmen.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:16.220
But Boba Fett really wins that award since,
for the most part, whoever fit into the armor

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.360
got to play him.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:21.221
Jeremy Bulloch played Fett through most of
the character's appearances in the Original

00:07:21.221 --> 00:07:25.460
Trilogy, with the exception of two days, when
he missed filming and the actor who played

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:28.169
the Rebel pilot Dak, John Morton, filled in.

00:07:28.169 --> 00:07:31.780
Throughout the Original Trilogy, Jason Wingreen
provided his voice.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:36.590
For the special editions, he was dubbed by
Temuera Morrison, the actor who played Jango

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:37.590
Fett.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:41.980
And when George Lucas needed more Fett footage
for his Special Editions, he decided to just

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:46.590
use three different Industrial Light and Magic
employees who happened to fit into the outfit.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:51.370
Finally, for the prequels, young Boba was
played by Daniel Logan, who also provided

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.639
the voice for Boba Fett in the Clone Wars
cartoon.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:58.650
And we're not even counting video games, radio
dramas, or Star Tours.

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:00.460
King of the Mandalorians

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:05.139
Though it's been wiped out by Star Wars' massive
continuity overhaul, Boba Fett was once the

00:08:05.139 --> 00:08:09.570
leader of his entire planet of Mandalore,
just like his father was before him.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:13.949
What's the name of the leader of all of Mandalore,
the fifth planet in the Mandalore system?

00:08:13.949 --> 00:08:15.470
Quite simply, "Mandalore."

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:20.180
That word probably works for everything — it's
like 'aloha,' 'shalom,' 'smurf,' or 'squanch.'

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.680
"Squanchy party bro!"

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:22.920
"Ah, Squanchy!"

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:26.100
"Is there a good place for me to SQUANCH around
here?"

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.570
"Squanchy you can squanch wherever you want,
man!"

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:33.839
The actual history of the Mandalorians seems
to shift around a lot, but in the 2008 Star

00:08:33.839 --> 00:08:38.469
Wars novel Legacy of the Force: Revelation,
Fett's reluctant rise to power is spelled

00:08:38.469 --> 00:08:39.469
out clearly.

00:08:39.469 --> 00:08:44.300
He's hired to kill the existing Mandalore
leader, Fenn Shysa, who ends up saving Fett's

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:47.399
life, but Shysa is critically injured in the
process.

00:08:47.399 --> 00:08:52.430
As a result, Fett is bound to honor his last
request: that Fett himself become the new

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:53.430
Mandalore...of Mandalore.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:58.671
As such, Fett had the Mandalorians fight back
against the alien Yuuzhan Vong invaders in

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:04.269
the novella Boba Fett: A Practical Man, and
helped restore Mandalore after the war.

00:09:04.269 --> 00:09:07.110
Make Mandalore great again, right?

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.199
Fett's family

00:09:08.199 --> 00:09:13.129
Another thing lost to Disney's revised continuity
was Fett's family, which he started sixteen

00:09:13.129 --> 00:09:14.769
years before A New Hope.

00:09:14.769 --> 00:09:19.329
It's weird to think of Fett as a doting dad,
but he and his bounty hunter wife, Sintas

00:09:19.329 --> 00:09:23.529
Vel, settled down and had a daughter named
Ailyn when Fett was only nineteen.

00:09:23.529 --> 00:09:29.089
Unfortunately for everyone, Sintas is assaulted
by Boba's boss, who Boba then kills, sending

00:09:29.089 --> 00:09:31.899
him spiralling into exile and divorce.

00:09:31.899 --> 00:09:36.750
Sintas ends up frozen in carbonite for four
decades, and their daughter goes on a misguided

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:38.920
quest to kill Boba Fett herself.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:43.470
Not only that, but Ailyn trains her own daughter,
Mirta, to follow in her footsteps.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.309
And you thought your family was messed up.

00:09:45.309 --> 00:09:49.889
All of that, and Boba Fett still found time
to train the Expanded Universe daughter of

00:09:49.889 --> 00:09:52.079
Han and Leia: Jaina Solo.

00:09:52.079 --> 00:09:56.179
With the help of Fett and his granddaughter
Mirta Gev, Jaina is able to kill her evil

00:09:56.179 --> 00:09:59.050
brother Jacen and restore peace to the galaxy.

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:03.589
So, no matter what reality you're following,
Han and Leia have one really messed up, evil

00:10:03.589 --> 00:10:04.589
kid.

00:10:04.589 --> 00:10:05.940
Those Skywalkers are bad news.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.259
Thanks for watching!

00:10:07.259 --> 00:10:10.079
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:10.079 --> 00:10:12.089
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

